    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seaman, sailor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				19.375
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				9.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.188
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				302a
			</span></i>, etc.: as Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ὅμιλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					921
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <i>by sea,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεζός</span> (by land), <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				719
			</span></i> (troch.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>passenger by sea,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύτην ἄγειν τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					901
				</span></i>
			: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συμποσίου ναῦται</span>
			<i>mates</i> in the drinking bout, <i><span class="en">
				Dionys.Eleg.
				5
			</span></i>.</div>
